    {"text": "Choking in adults: If person can cough forcefully, encourage coughing. If cannot cough, speak, or breathe: 1. Give 5 firm back blows between shoulder blades with heel of hand. 2. If ineffective: give 5 abdominal thrusts (Heimlich manoeuvre) — stand behind, arms around waist, one hand fist just above navel, sharp inward-upward thrust. Alternate back blows and abdominal thrusts. Call emergency if unsuccessful. For infants: different technique — seek training.", "source": "NHS First Aid", "topic": "choking", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/first-aid/choking-adult-first-aid/", "language": "en"},

